      "title": "Request query evaluated as JavaScript",
      "description": "The /calc handler passes req.query.expr straight to eval. The added comments switch off the lint checks that would report this line. Any caller of /calc can run arbitrary JavaScript inside the server process. That caller can read secrets, touch files and spawn processes. Parse expr with a restricted arithmetic evaluator such as expr-eval, or with a small hand-written parser. Remove the disable comments.",
