      "title": "Shell command built from upload name",
      "description": "make_thumbnail puts upload_name into a shell command string and runs it with shell=True. Its docstring says the upload form supplies the name. A user who uploads a file named with shell metacharacters runs commands on the server. A name containing ../ also writes outside THUMB_DIR. Pass an argument list to subprocess.run without shell=True. Reject names that are not a plain basename.",
      "suggested_change": "    subprocess.run([\"convert\", f\"{UPLOAD_DIR}/{upload_name}\", \"-resize\", \"128x128\", f\"{THUMB_DIR}/{upload_name}\"], check=True)",
      "source": "semgrep:python.lang.security.audit.subprocess-shell-true.subprocess-shell-true",
      "candidate": "c1",
